{"kind":"request","text":"Security R14 (6dd06d03 sections 2.3 and 5): usage against configuration.\n\nWork:\n1. scripts/usage-report.mjs queries 30 days of METRICS route points (place, answer) through the analytics SQL API, with an API token read from stdin. It lists, for each Worker, the routes and platform versions that were never used. It never prints or stores the token.\n2. The dormant pieces named in 2.3 appear in the list when unused: the GitHub port, the ScopeService entrypoint with no binding, the demo creation route, and the always-bound Artifacts, R2, metrics and console logging.\n\nWitness: the script, run against a recorded sample of route points, lists exactly the unused routes and versions of the sample.\n\nThe planner runs the script with the operator token and files retirement requests from its output. Closes the inventory step of 2.3.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 10 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"A script that lists unused routes and platform versions per Worker from METRICS; the planner runs it and files retirements; closes 2.3 inventory step. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}